## Which definitions a library exports (ImplementationPlan.md M22.a item 2,
## Q22; 5.9.15; M22.b item 2 for aliases; recon p2/exports-multiasm.md
## 10.1). Candidates are the defined GLOBAL and WEAK symbols with DEFAULT or
## PROTECTED visibility, COMMON symbols included as data:
## - hidden definitions stay in <Module> and are not exported;
## - on Windows triples, when some input defines a dllexport symbol (here in
##   one object of two), only the dllexport candidates are exported, unless
##   --export-all-symbols; without any dllexport, every candidate is
##   (GNU ld's auto-export rule);
## - --exclude-libs=<list> (lld/ELF's option: archive names separated by ','
##   or ':') and --exclude-libs=ALL keep the members of those archives out;
## - commons (one export for two tentative definitions), weak functions and
##   variables are exported;
## - a function alias becomes a forwarding method of its own name, whose
##   accessor returns the aliasee's '<msil>fn_' field (an alias has no field
##   of its own); a data alias's accessor returns the aliasee's address field
##   plus its offset;
## - a thread-local candidate (a variable in '.tdata') is
##   'thread-local storage is not supported yet: <s> in <file>';
## - COMDAT copies (section 12 row 'Q22 as implemented (what never exports;
##   ...)' of 2026-10-26): on Windows triples a candidate that is not
##   dllexport and belongs to a COMDAT group of its object (a function that
##   is a member, or a variable whose segment is one) is never exported, by
##   the automatic rule or by --export-all-symbols: an MSVC string literal
##   ('??_C@...'), a selectany variable (weak_odr in a comdat) and a
##   linkonce_odr inline function; they stay private to the library (the
##   function in <Module>), and the symbol table lists none of them. A weak definition outside a COMDAT group
##   (w) is still exported, a dllexport COMDAT function exports as before,
##   and ELF triples export COMDAT members as any definition. A program that
##   has its own copy of such an inline function links against the library
##   without a warning (nothing was exported to shadow).
## listing.py prints the export class's members without bodies, or one
## method with its body.

# REQUIRES: llvm-cil-dump
# RUN: rm -rf %t && split-file %s %t && cd %t
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj vis.ll -o vis.o
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj vis2.ll -o vis2.o
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj win.ll -o win.o
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj other.ll -o other.o
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj api.ll -o api.o
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj xm.ll -o xm.o
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj ym.ll -o ym.o
# RUN: llc -filetype=obj tls.ll -o tls.o
# RUN: llvm-ar rc libx.a xm.o
# RUN: llvm-ar rc liby.a ym.o

# DEFINE: %{fc} = FileCheck %s --implicit-check-not="PLEASE submit" --implicit-check-not="Stack dump" \
# DEFINE:   --implicit-check-not="LLVM ERROR"
# DEFINE: %{listing} = %python %S/Inputs/shared/listing.py

## Visibility, commons, weak definitions and aliases (an ELF triple).
# RUN: msil-ld -shared vis.o vis2.o -o vis.dll 2>&1 | count 0
# RUN: llvm-cil-dump vis.dll > vis.txt
# RUN: %{listing} members vis.txt vis | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=VIS
